1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,740
Good morning.
Harbour Bike Tours, Sophie speaking.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:07,580
Hi, my name's Liam. I'm calling about
booking a tour for a group of friends.

3
00:00:07,959 --> 00:00:09,920
Great! How many of you will there be?

4
00:00:10,855 --> 00:00:14,620
Well, originally it was six.
Then my cousin dropped out,

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,460
and yesterday someone else said they
couldn't make it. So we're down to four.

6
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,860
And do you know which tour you'd like?

7
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:23,800
Not really. What do most people go for?

8
00:00:24,185 --> 00:00:26,353
A lot of people assume
it's the Harbour Tour,

9
00:00:26,377 --> 00:00:28,412
because that's the
one on all our posters.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,080
But the one that always
sells out first is the food tour.

11
00:00:32,425 --> 00:00:35,400
We're leaning towards the harbour one.
How long is it?

12
00:00:36,349 --> 00:00:39,124
It's advertised as half
a day, but realistically

13
00:00:39,148 --> 00:00:41,412
you're back here in
around three hours.

14
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:42,860
And where do we meet?

15
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,440
At the shop. We're on the waterfront. If
you're standing outside the ferry terminal,

16
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,860
we're just across the
road, next to the bank.

17
00:00:50,239 --> 00:00:51,360
What time does it start?

18
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,320
The morning ride used to leave at
nine, but because of the ferry traffic,

19
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,960
we've put it back by half an hour.

20
00:00:57,359 --> 00:00:59,860
We were hoping to come
at the very start of next week.

21
00:01:00,145 --> 00:01:01,867
Not on the Monday, I'm afraid.

22
00:01:01,891 --> 00:01:05,272
That's the one day we don't
open. Any other day is fine.

23
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,565
And the price?

24
00:01:06,859 --> 00:01:11,280
The night tour is $50, and
the harbour one is $65 each.

25
00:01:11,589 --> 00:01:14,360
One of us is still at university.
Is there any reduction?

26
00:01:14,819 --> 00:01:17,602
There is, as long as they
bring their student card along.

27
00:01:17,626 --> 00:01:19,552
A letter from the
college isn't enough.

28
00:01:19,929 --> 00:01:21,249
Is there anything we should wear?

29
00:01:21,489 --> 00:01:23,925
For safety, no
sandals or flip-flops.

30
00:01:23,949 --> 00:01:27,739
You need something that
covers your toes. So closed shoes.

31
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:29,740
We'll bring sunscreen, obviously.

32
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:31,488
Good. And a light jacket too.

33
00:01:31,512 --> 00:01:35,132
It gets surprisingly chilly by
the water, even in summer.

34
00:01:35,269 --> 00:01:38,340
The night tour sounds fun as well.
Where does that one end up?

35
00:01:38,489 --> 00:01:40,968
It starts here and finishes
at the night market.

36
00:01:40,992 --> 00:01:42,932
Most people stay
on there for dinner.

37
00:01:43,244 --> 00:01:44,700
Is it as long as the harbour tour?

38
00:01:44,994 --> 00:01:47,920
No. It's an hour shorter. Two hours.

39
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,260
Cycling in the dark sounds a bit risky.

40
00:01:50,624 --> 00:01:54,660
Every bike has lights fitted, front
and back. So you'll be quite safe.

41
00:01:55,019 --> 00:01:56,880
I did try to book on your website.

42
00:01:57,199 --> 00:01:59,782
The website's only for
individuals. Groups have to

43
00:01:59,806 --> 00:02:02,712
arrange it over the phone.
So you're in the right place.

44
00:02:03,029 --> 00:02:04,420
What happens if the weather's bad?

45
00:02:04,829 --> 00:02:07,587
If we have to cancel, we'll
move you to another day.

46
00:02:07,611 --> 00:02:11,112
And if none of the other dates
suit you, you'll get a full refund.

47
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,760
My nephew's 11. Could he come along?

48
00:02:14,084 --> 00:02:16,820
Sorry. Riders have to be at least 12.

49
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:19,800
A couple of us haven't
been on a bike in years.

50
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,628
That's very common.
Before you set off, there's a

51
00:02:22,652 --> 00:02:25,152
practice session in the
car park behind the shop.

52
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,440
Who leads the tours?

53
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:30,208
The rotor isn't out yet. It
could be Maria, but I'd say

54
00:02:30,232 --> 00:02:33,612
it'll most likely be Tony.
He takes most of the groups.

55
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:35,140
Is there parking near you?

56
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:39,832
There's a small car park, but it's expensive
and the buses aren't very frequent.

57
00:02:40,404 --> 00:02:44,120
Most of our customers come by train.
The station's five minutes walk away.

58
00:02:44,404 --> 00:02:46,400
And how much do we pay when we book?

59
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:51,000
We take 20% of the total up
front and the rest on the day.

60
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,760
Great. Let's go ahead.

61
00:02:53,045 --> 00:02:55,200
Wonderful. I'll set that up for you now.

